{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446118-how-much-quintessence","id":1446118,"title":"How much Quintessence?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-27T10:37:31-07:00","id":1446118,"title":"How much Quintessence?","content":"On my ongoing quest to understanding Prime Magic I have come across a somewhat basic question that I can't wrap my head around.<br /> <br /> Quintessence is described as a very scarce resource, yet it has many in-game uses and a whole Sphere focusing (among other things) on manipulating it. So the question is:<br /> <br /> How scarce are we talking exactly?<br /> <br /> More specifically:<br /> <br /> - Are smaller nodes common? Is any place where people pour their emotion, thoughts, hopes and the like a node? Basically, is every reasonable church, school gym, tribunal, graveyard a node?<br /> <br /> - How often does a Prime-less Mage get to refuel his Quintessence pool?<br /> <br /> - Is Tass found commonly in possession of sleepers? Can Mages walk in an antiquarian shop and just <i><b>buy</b></i> Tass?<br /> <br /> - On a more mechanical note, just <i><b>how much</b></i> reality is a point of Quintessence worth, and how much can you extract by &quot;burning&quot; common things? I as wooden chair, for instance, worth a point of Quintessence? Does it always cost one single point to create both a goldfish or an elephant (given the appropriate proficiency in Life magic)?<br /> <br /> How do you usually rule it? How much Quintessence do you usually let flow in your games and how much do you think is a reasonable amount?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26807-nemogg","name":"NemoGG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"